.TH GETSYS 1.SH NAMEgetsys \- show the system global variables.SH SYNOPSIS\fBgetsys\fR.SH DESCRIPTION\fBgetsys\fRprints OS-9's system globals, one to a line with its meaning: the OS-9version, the init module's address, ticks per second, the date, whetherthere is a floating-point coprocessor, the module directory and theprocess and path descriptor tables, and some ninety more..nf    System global variables (OS-9/680x0 V2.3):    number of ticks per second .................. 100    0 = no FPU, 1 = 68881, 2 = 68882 ............ 1.fi.PPWhere a variable has no value on the system it is running on it says soon the error output, so\fB2>/nil\fRleaves only the table.  It takes no options..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOshdev, modinfo